		summary = "**Fresh water** or **freshwater** is any naturally occurring liquid or frozen [[Water|water]] containing low [[Concentration|concentrations]] of dissolved [[Salt (chemistry)|salts]] and other total dissolved solids. The term excludes [[Seawater|seawater]] and [[Brackish water|brackish water]], but it does include non-salty mineral-rich waters, such as chalybeate springs. Fresh water may encompass frozen and meltwater in [[Ice sheet|ice sheets]], [[Ice cap|ice caps]], [[Glacier|glaciers]], snowfields and [[Iceberg|icebergs]], natural [[Precipitation|precipitations]] such as [[Rain|rainfall]], snowfall, [[Hail|hail]]/sleet and graupel, and [[Surface runoff|surface runoffs]] that form inland bodies of water such as [[Wetland|wetlands]], [[Pond|ponds]], [[Lake|lakes]], [[River|rivers]], [[Stream|streams]], as well as [[Groundwater|groundwater]] contained in [[Aquifer|aquifers]], subterranean rivers and lakes.",
